   "k": "8eaarh",
   "en": "Communist China"
  },
  {
   "k": "1gcplnd",
   "en": "When the Chinese Civil War resumed in 1946, the Soviet-backed Second East Turkestan Republic was formed in Sinkiang and attempted to become independent of the Nationalist government, siding with the communists and peacefully integrating into the newly formed People's Republic of China. Sheng Shicai went into exile in Taiwan with the rest of the Kuomintang."
  },
